    methodsH3: 'How each result was produced',
    methods: (): [string, Part[]][] => [
      ['WBCIC-SHU baselines', ['The publisher’s processed derivative: 58 anonymous channel indices at 250 Hz in four-second epochs. Welch relative band power in 4–8, 8–13, 13–30 and 30–40 Hz per channel, as log ratios: 232 values per trial. A StandardScaler fitted on session 1 only, then a RidgeClassifier (alpha 1, no class weights). No hyperparameter search, target normalization, calibration or abstention.']],
      ['WBCIC-SHU, frozen CBraMod', ['The same trials, resampled to 200 Hz and zero-padded to 800 samples; each trial and channel divided by its own standard deviation, a dimensionless input, not the checkpoint’s native amplitude, so upstream benchmark numbers are not reproduced. CBraMod in evaluation mode with every weight frozen; its four temporal patch embeddings averaged into 11,600 values per trial; a separate StandardScaler and RidgeClassifier fitted on each person’s session 1 only. No backbone training, LoRA or target-session calibration.']],
      ['Longitudinal RSVP', ['57 EEG channels, −200 to +700 ms around each event, baseline-normalized; six 100 ms averages from +100 to +700 ms, 342 values per event. Per person, first-visit blocks 1–3 fit a fixed L2 logistic regression and block 4 fits Platt calibration; later visits are scored on blocks 2–4. Group B is not used. No hyperparameter search, target-label calibration, fine-tuning or LoRA.']],
      ['Continuous cursor tracking', ['62 channels at 1,000 Hz, already band-passed and notch-filtered by the publisher. Five bands from 4 to 30 Hz through a per-trial FIR filter, the preceding second of band power as channel-relative log power: 310 values per row, from a trial-contained 2-second past window, every 40 ms. Per response arm, a StandardScaler and response scaling fitted on the earliest session only, then Ridge (alpha 1). No tuning, LoRA, target-session calibration or foundation-model inference.']],
    ],
    intervalsH3: 'What the intervals cover',
    limitsH3: 'Limits that hold for all four results',
    intervals: 'Every interval is a pointwise 95% percentile interval from 10,000 participant (or, for cursor tracking, record) bootstrap resamples within its cohort, with paired draws for every difference. Each is conditional on the fixed trained models and predictions: refitting, preprocessing, model and protocol selection — and, for CBraMod, pretraining overlap — are not included, and there is no multiple-comparison adjustment.',
    limits: [
      'The same person in every result. Each decoder is trained on that person’s own earlier labelled data; none of this measures a decoder on someone it has never seen, or on another dataset.',
      'Offline only. No real-time, closed-loop, clinical or deployment claim, and in cursor tracking no claim about online control quality or intended-motion decoding.',
      'Nothing pooled, nothing ranked. The three datasets, the two WBCIC-SHU cohorts, the two cursor-tracking cohorts and its two response arms are each reported apart; no single score summarises them, and none joins the eight-protocol core matrix.',
      'Fixed protocols, frozen before scoring; the scores here were not used to tune them. The CBraMod arm is the exception that is disclosed: it was frozen after the spectral ridge results existed and reuses their test trials.',
      'Target labels and metadata had been seen. Earlier WBCIC-SHU schema checks inspected label domains and counts, and RSVP event roles and target labels were inspected during quality checks. Every prediction was sealed before scoring, and no target label entered normalization, fitting, calibration, prediction or any hyperparameter, threshold, abstention or retry decision.',
      'Publisher preprocessing as delivered. WBCIC-SHU’s channel order rests on the publisher’s procedures and the raw headers, not a direct raw-to-processed proof, and its physical amplitude is unresolved. The selection history and temporal support of its reference, filter, epoch and baseline choices are not fully established.',
      'No calibration arm. Neither WBCIC-SHU result says whether a few labelled session-3 trials would help: that needs its own matched arm, and none was run (no LoRA or calibration-budget comparison either).',
      'Cursor tracking: session, practice, speed and the historical decoder in use are confounded, and the recorded decoder labels are observational contexts, not randomized comparisons; the unknown order of decoders within a session rules out chronological-prefix and online-adaptation claims. A source-only stability diagnostic would be a new, separately frozen analysis, not a revision of these scores.',
      'Audit scope. Each result passed an independent numerical audit of its saved predictions, metrics and intervals; none independently repeated the full feature extraction from the raw EEG, and for CBraMod the encoder was not rerun on all the EEG.',
    ],
